      {
        "rank": 8,
        "evidence_text": "Marking of Joker Tyres is subject to the penalties listed in the table in Attachment 8. However, Competitors need to report to the technical delegate the use of joker tyres for remarking and accounting purpose.\n\nFor the avoidance of doubt teams must declare for which session each joker tyre(s) will be used and latest 60 mins before the session in question.\n\nThe penalties will be issued according to the attachment 8 tyre-table.\n\nIn case of a change of weather conditions and wet weather tyres have been used instead of the Joker Tyres the penalty for that grid remains but the joker tyres are now part of the marked tyres without any penalty for the next session. If the driver does not take part in the session for which the joker tyres have been declared then the competitor re-register the joker tyres for the next session at the same event and will be subject to the corresponding penalty\n\nneeds to according to the attachment 8 tyre-table.\n\nIn case the competitor has not used the declared joker tyre(s) during the declared session the joker tyre(s) must be declared again and used in the next session of the same event and subject to the penalty according to the attachment 8 tyre-table.",
